2.6.4. An automaton performing random walks
Let F be defined on the alphabet A = (Z/2Z)2 on the neighbourhood {−2, . . . , 2} by the local rule
f defined as follows:
                                                                    1 if (a−1 , b−1 ) = (1, 1) or (a0 , b0 ) = (0, 1);
